It is Tuesday morning.
I go into a small kiosk.
A man stands behind the counter.
"Hello, how can I help?" he asks.
"I would like to buy a Danish SIM card," I say.
"I need a phone number."
He smiles and gives me a small package.
I pay and put the card in my phone.
Now it works.
I read my new number out loud.
It is twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight.
Now I finally have a number in Denmark.
